{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791429060,"nonce":"sBg0oJUyLPoSC7mFLfWwdIrY7Zk=","title":"Any promotions mix boxed values with raw scalar and reference slots","message":"Issue5322 reaches a native crash at fault address 0x5 after its macro typing diagnostics are corrected. Its Array\u003cAny\u003e string element is boxed, but promotion to String hands the box to string equality. A function declared to return Any also needs the same boxed representation as assignments and array elements.\n\nThe native-valid regression AnyValues.hx additionally covers implicit return and assignment promotions, scalar arguments, mixed arrays, fields, abstract-backed strings and null. In the v5 experiment, Issue5322 passes seven assertions but the regression still fails at \"Any argument\": a pointer-typed Any parameter is treated as raw scalar bits by the optional-return coercion. The Any field named value also triggers a fallback scan that selects an unrelated erased-I64 field, and stores an unboxed payload instead of the Any box.\n\nRelevant boundaries: mir/helpers/boxing.rs, mir/expr/casts.rs, mir/stmt/statements.rs and mir/field/lvalue.rs. Native evidence: /tmp/rayzor-any-values-native-v1.log. Runtime and MIR evidence: /tmp/rayzor-any-values-pinned-v4.log, /tmp/rayzor-any-values-mir-v4.log, /tmp/rayzor-any-values-mir-v5.log and /tmp/rayzor-macro-probe-focus-v5/report.tsv. Typing diagnostics are tracked under 7d98b4af7e339634383cc66ebc1bdfe349f7b5ae90c0c9447219b0b133db72c4.","files":null}]}